    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Pyrenean kingdom that took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#zaragoza">Zaragoza</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ebro-river">Ebro</a> valley from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> in the twelfth century.</li><li>Petronila's marriage to the count of Barcelona created the Crown of Aragon, which later joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a> to form <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#spain">Spain</a>.</li><li>Its Cortes, fueros and the Justicia limited royal power until Philip V abolished them in 1707.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ramiro II, a monk called from the cloister to the throne in 1134, married to provide an heir and retired to monastic life once his baby daughter Petronila was betrothed.</p></aside>
    </section>

